---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SchemaBench from "../components/SchemaBench.astro";
---

<Base title="Plinth Schema — repair and validate LLM JSON" description="Repair malformed JSON from LLMs, then validate against JSON Schema. Open-source core @plinth/schema." path="/schema">
  <div class="land-band" style="display:inline-block">Bearing · Schema</div>
  <h1>Make the model’s JSON land on the chart</h1>
  <p class="lede">LLMs return fences, trailing commas, single quotes, Python <code class="inline-code">True</code>, and truncated braces. Schema repairs them, then proves the result against JSON Schema.</p>

  <div style="margin-top:2rem">
    <SchemaBench />
  </div>

  <section class="prose" style="margin-top:2rem">
    <h2>API</h2>
    <pre class="mono" style="background:#063a42;padding:1rem;overflow:auto">{`curl -X POST https://api.plinth.dev/v1/schema/repair-and-validate \\
  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\
  -d '{"text":"{ok: True}", "schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"ok":{"type":"boolean"}}}}'`}</pre>
    <p>Also available as MCP tools at <code class="inline-code">/mcp</code>.</p>
    <p><a href="/docs/schema">Schema docs</a> · <a href="/guides/llm-json-repair">LLM JSON repair guide</a> · <a href="/pricing">Pricing</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>
